{"agent":"main","body":{"args_hash":"sha256:825e0a9b9e958e22f35178cfa209100ea5b6bcb9bc6e2cd8bb1cd975985ec98c","args_inline":{"content":"---\nname: project-fx-rounding-bug\ndescription: ledger/fx.py convert() used int() truncation causing cumulative EUR reconcile mismatches\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\n`ledger/fx.py:convert()` used `int(cents * rate)`, which truncates toward zero instead of rounding. Across thousands of postings into the EUR account (4471), this systematically biased conversions downward, accumulating to a -0.30 EUR mismatch in `python3 -m ledger.reconcile fixtures` against `fixtures/controls.csv`. All other (USD-only, rate=1.0) accounts were unaffected since truncation only matters when the rate is non-integer.\n\n**Why:** Only account 4471 uses a non-1.0 FX rate (EUR), so this class of rounding bug only shows up on multi-currency accounts — worth checking first when a single account is off by a small cumulative amount and others reconcile clean.\n\n**How to apply:** Fixed by switching to `round(cents * rate)` (banker's rounding) in [[fx.py]]. If similar rounding-drift bugs reappear elsewhere in this codebase, check any place doing `int(x * rate)` style truncation on minor-unit currency amounts.\n","file_path":"/var/folders/yb/b_617z_s2ml933nmr_k7m47m0000gn/T/saga-bench-1958376525/py-0010-ledger-fx-rounding/1/cfg/claude-config/projects/-private-var-folders-yb-b-617z-s2ml933nmr-k7m47m0000gn-T-saga-bench-1958376525-py-0010-ledger-fx-rounding-1-ws/memory/project_fx_rounding_bug.md"},"component":"harness","cwd_rel":".","index_version":null,"tool":"Write","tool_use_id":"toolu_013Mxc7e6fttQpKUQuFhxY8J"},"hash":"sha256:eb0797c1bb8620c99ecc78b09e980af8c3a7b784ca959dbf9e175ee5d5ce86fa","mono_ns":31000000,"prev":"sha256:225ab48aed689deca58bd0bcf940b01f20fc12a8fa6d760e8c88aace8c1ea798","schema":"saga.trace/1","seq":31,"session":"878bbc09-8bfc-4b13-bb85-70f57c6719c9","source":"stream-json","ts":"2026-01-01T00:00:00.031Z","turn":1,"type":"tool_call"}
